@page
@model IndexModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Home";
}

<section id="hero-banner" class="hero-section">
    <div class="container hero-content">
        <p class="hero-eyebrow">Computing &bull; Design &bull; Networking</p>
        <h1>Where Innovation Meets Craftsmanship</h1>
        <p class="hero-lead">
            Established in 1989 in central Sheffield, Kasper College equips students with the knowledge,
            technical prowess, and creative problem-solving skills required to succeed in a rapidly evolving global market.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
            <a asp-page="/Courses/Index" class="btn btn-gold">Explore 2027/28 Courses</a>
            <a asp-page="/Business" class="btn btn-outline-light">Partner With Us</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section-block" aria-labelledby="stats-heading">
    <div class="container">
        <h2 id="stats-heading">Key Facts &amp; Statistics</h2>
        <div class="grid-cards stats-grid">
            <article class="card stat-card">
                <h3>9,500 m&sup2;</h3>
                <p>Of modern, purpose-built educational space in central Sheffield.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card stat-card">
                <h3>1,600+ Students</h3>
                <p>Undergraduate and postgraduate students from more than 40 countries.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card stat-card">
                <h3>240+ Staff</h3>
                <p>Dedicated academic faculty, industry-fellow lecturers, and specialized technical support staff.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card stat-card">
                <h3>96% Employability</h3>
                <p>Graduates in professional employment or further study within six months of graduation.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card stat-card">
                <h3>&pound;4.5 Million</h3>
                <p>Recently invested in state-of-the-art GPU clusters, cybersecurity cyber ranges, and VR/AR immersive labs.</p>
            </article>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section-block section-alt" aria-labelledby="about-heading">
    <div class="container two-col">
        <div>
            <h2 id="about-heading">About Kasper College</h2>
            <p>
                Kasper College was established in 1989 to specialize in Computing, Design, and Digital Technologies.
                Over the past three decades, we have evolved into one of the region's premier technical and creative education hubs.
                At Kasper College, we are dedicated to providing students with the education, hands-on experience, and industry exposure
                they need to achieve their career aspirations.
            </p>
            <p>
                Our close integration with leading technology firms, software houses, creative agencies, and regional enterprises
                provides students with direct industry pathways, live commercial briefs, and invaluable placement opportunities.
                Kasper College gives you the definitive edge when entering the professional world.
            </p>
            <figure class="media-figure">
                <img src="~/images/image1.jpg" alt="Students collaborating inside Kasper College campus atrium" />
                <figcaption>Purpose-built collaborative learning spaces at Kasper College, Sheffield.</figcaption>
            </figure>
        </div>

        <aside class="card principal-card" aria-labelledby="principal-heading">
            <h3 id="principal-heading">Principal's Welcome</h3>
            <blockquote class="principal-quote">
                "Welcome to Kasper College. Whether you are stepping into higher education for the first time, advancing your skills
                through postgraduate study, or collaborating with us as an industry partner, Kasper College offers an exceptional community
                of passionate educators, researchers, and creators. Our campus in Sheffield has been purposefully designed to foster collaboration
                between computing specialists and creative designers&mdash;mirroring the modern digital economy. We look forward to supporting you on your journey to excellence."
            </blockquote>
            <p><strong>Dr. Marcus Vance</strong>, Principal &amp; CEO</p>

            <h3>Our Mission, Vision &amp; Core Values</h3>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Mission:</strong> To empower students from all backgrounds through inspiring teaching, cutting-edge technical facilities, and innovative research in computing, networking, and creative design.</li>
                <li><strong>Vision:</strong> To be recognised globally as a benchmark institution where technology meets creativity, preparing ethical, skilled, and visionary digital leaders.</li>
                <li><strong>Innovation &amp; Exploration:</strong> We cultivate curiosity, experimentation, and critical thinking across digital and creative domains.</li>
                <li><strong>Industry Relevance:</strong> Every course is built in consultation with industry partners to ensure curriculum alignment with modern tech stacks and workplace practices.</li>
                <li><strong>Inclusivity &amp; Community:</strong> We champion diversity, accessibility, and mutual support across our vibrant campus.</li>
            </ul>
        </aside>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section-block" aria-labelledby="departments-heading">
    <div class="container">
        <h2 id="departments-heading">Academic Departments &amp; Course Pathways</h2>
        <div class="grid-cards two-col">
            <article class="card">
                <img src="~/images/image2.jpg" alt="High-performance computing workstation setup" class="card-img" />
                <h3>1. Department of Computing &amp; Digital Technologies</h3>
                <p>
                    The Department of Computing offers a comprehensive spectrum of undergraduate, postgraduate, and foundation programmes
                    designed to suit applicants with diverse educational backgrounds. Whether you aim to build scalable distributed architectures,
                    secure critical infrastructure against cyber threats, or engineer engaging game engines, our courses combine deep theoretical rigor with industry-standard tooling.
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Core Computing Disciplines:</strong> Computer Science, Software Engineering, Cyber Security with Forensics, Computer Networks, and Computer Science for Games.</li>
                    <li><strong>Postgraduate Programmes:</strong> MSc Computing (conversion pathway for non-computing graduates), MSc Cyber Security, and MPhil Computing and Informatics.</li>
                    <li><strong>Foundation Years:</strong> Dedicated 4-year programmes providing foundational maths, programming, and web technology principles for students looking to build their entry qualifications.</li>
                </ul>
                <a asp-page="/Courses/Index" class="btn btn-primary">Browse Computing Courses</a>
            </article>

            <article class="card">
                <img src="~/images/image3.jpg" alt="Creative design studio with digital drawing displays" class="card-img" />
                <h3>2. Department of Art, Design &amp; Media</h3>
                <p>
                    The Department of Art, Design &amp; Media forms an internationally connected creative community housed under one roof.
                    We encourage interdisciplinary exploration, speculative design, and innovative craftsmanship. Our art and design courses
                    don't just train you in software; they foster alternative ways of thinking, making, communicating, and challenging contemporary culture.
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Core Design Disciplines:</strong> Graphic Design, Interior Architecture and Design, Game Design and Development, Digital Media Production, Product Design (BA &amp; BSc routes), and Jewellery, Materials &amp; Design.</li>
                    <li><strong>Studio Culture:</strong> Students enjoy personal studio spaces, collaborative critique areas, and daily access to specialized digital fabrication and traditional making workshops.</li>
                </ul>
                <a asp-page="/Courses/Index" class="btn btn-primary">Browse Art &amp; Design Courses</a>
            </article>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section-block section-alt" aria-labelledby="facilities-overview-heading">
    <div class="container">
        <h2 id="facilities-overview-heading">Campus Facilities Overview</h2>
        <p>
            The College is located in an attractive, recently refurbished architectural complex featuring light-filled spaces,
            energy-efficient environmental systems, and cutting-edge digital infrastructure spanning 9,500 m&sup2;.
        </p>
        <div class="grid-cards">
            <article class="card">
                <h3>High-Performance Computing Laboratories</h3>
                <p>Specialist labs featuring dual-boot Linux/Windows workstations, dedicated GPU compute nodes for machine learning, data science, and graphics rendering.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card">
                <h3>Cybersecurity Operations Centre (SOC) &amp; Cyber Range</h3>
                <p>An isolated, sandboxed networking environment designed for penetration testing, threat hunting, malware analysis, and real-time defense simulations.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card">
                <h3>Network Engineering Suites</h3>
                <p>Full-height Cisco enterprise server racks, hardware switches, routers, fiber termination stations, and IoT testbeds.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card">
                <h3>Creative Design Studios &amp; Digital Media Suites</h3>
                <p>Spacious, natural-light studios equipped with 27-inch Apple iMacs, Wacom Cintiq interactive pen displays, and full Adobe Creative Cloud suites.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card">
                <h3>3D Prototyping &amp; Fabrication Workshop</h3>
                <p>Equipped with multi-material 3D printers, laser cutters, CNC milling machines, vacuum formers, and electronics assembly benches.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card">
                <h3>Virtual &amp; Augmented Reality (VR/AR) Immersion Lab</h3>
                <p>Featuring Meta Quest Pro, HTC Vive Focus 3 headsets, high-precision motion capture cameras, and spatial audio testing gear.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card">
                <h3>Double-Height 300-Seat Lecture Theatre</h3>
                <p>Equipped with dual 4K laser projection, immersive acoustic treatment, live video streaming, and automated lecture capture systems.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card">
                <h3>Dramatic Three-Storey Glass Open Atrium</h3>
                <p>The social heart of the campus, featuring expansive exhibition areas, student showcases, informal breakout seating, and natural daylight.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card">
                <h3>Collaborative Study Pods &amp; Project Rooms</h3>
                <p>Bookable student team rooms equipped with 75-inch interactive touchscreens, wireless screen casting, and video conferencing hardware.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card">
                <h3>Library and Learning Resource Centre (LRC)</h3>
                <p>Open 24/7 during term time, providing quiet research carrels, extensive digital repository access, bookable pods, and equipment loan services.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card">
                <h3>The Atrium Cafe &amp; Coffee Lounge</h3>
                <p>Serving freshly prepared meals, barista coffee, healthy grab-and-go options, and dietary-tailored catering.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card">
                <h3>Contemporary Art &amp; Design Gallery</h3>
                <p>A public exhibition space hosting seasonal student degree shows, faculty retrospectives, and guest industry exhibitions.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card">
                <h3>Accessibility &amp; Inclusive Campus Features</h3>
                <p>Fully accessible campus with ramped entrances, automatic doors, multi-floor elevators, accessible restrooms on every level, hearing assistance induction loops, and dedicated Blue Badge parking.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card">
                <h3>Green Travel Hub &amp; Cycle Storage</h3>
                <p>Secure swipe-card access cycle storage for 120+ bicycles, maintenance stands, tyre inflation points, and individual student lockers and shower facilities.</p>
            </article>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section-block" aria-labelledby="hours-heading">
    <div class="container two-col">
        <article class="card">
            <h2 id="hours-heading">Campus Opening Hours &amp; Term Dates</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Main Building Opening Hours:</strong> Monday &ndash; Friday: 07:30 &ndash; 22:00 | Saturday &ndash; Sunday: 08:30 &ndash; 18:00</li>
                <li><strong>Library &amp; Resource Centre Hours:</strong> 24 Hours keycard access 7 days a week during term-time for registered students and staff.</li>
                <li><strong>Autumn Term 2026/27:</strong> 28 September 2026 &ndash; 18 December 2026 (Reading Week: 02 November &ndash; 06 November 2026)</li>
                <li><strong>Spring Term 2026/27:</strong> 11 January 2027 &ndash; 26 March 2027 (Reading Week: 15 February &ndash; 19 February 2027)</li>
                <li><strong>Summer Term 2026/27:</strong> 19 April 2027 &ndash; 25 June 2027 (Assessment &amp; Degree Showcase Period: 17 May &ndash; 11 June 2027)</li>
            </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
            <h2>Transport &amp; Travel Guide</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>By Train:</strong> Sheffield Central Station is a 12-minute walk from the main entrance, or a 5-minute ride on the Supertram.</li>
                <li><strong>By Supertram:</strong> Take the Blue or Yellow route to the 'College Square / Arts Quarter' tram stop located directly opposite the campus plaza.</li>
                <li><strong>By Bus:</strong> Major bus routes 51, 52, 120, and X1 terminate or stop directly outside the Main Entrance on Main Street.</li>
                <li><strong>By Car:</strong> Easily accessible from the M1 Motorway (Junction 33) via the Sheffield Parkway. Note: On-campus parking is strictly reserved for Blue Badge holders and authorized college visitors. Public parking is available at the adjacent City Gateway Multi-Storey Car Park.</li>
                <li><strong>By Bicycle:</strong> Located adjacent to National Cycle Route 6. Secure swipe-card indoor bike storage and shower facilities are located on Ground Floor West.</li>
            </ul>
        </article>
    </div>
</section>
